ggml-cpu/spacemit: initialise every running max in the decode flash-attention kernel

flash_attn_ext_f16_one_chunk_inner_vlen1024_vf16_mrow<QLEN> declared

    float M[QLEN] = { -INFINITY };

Aggregate initialisation sets only M[0] to -INFINITY; M[1..QLEN-1] start at 0.
For query heads 1..QLEN-1 of a GQA group the online softmax then starts with a
running maximum of 0, the weights exp(s - 0) of negative scores are converted
to _Float16 for the fp16 V accumulator and underflow, while the sum S stays in
float: the head output is scaled down and distorted. The tiled (batched) kernel
initialises M[i] = -INFINITY in a loop and is not affected.

Symptom: token-by-token decode (n_ubatch = 1) on the SpacemiT IME2 path gives
duplicated sub-word tokens; KLD to the F16 model 0.286 instead of ~0.05.

Applies with `git apply` or `patch -p1` to llama.cpp 0a1ef30 (b11796) and to
master f5222f2 (2026-10-28), where the file is unchanged.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/spacemit/rvv_kernels.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/spacemit/rvv_kernels.cpp
@@ -666,7 +666,8 @@
                                                                   size_t              tcm_buffer_size) {
     GGML_ASSERT(flash_attn_ext_supported_shape_vlen1024_vf16(DK, DV));
     float S[QLEN] = { 0.0f };       // sum
-    float M[QLEN] = { -INFINITY };  // maximum KQ value
+    float M[QLEN];                  // maximum KQ value
+    std::fill(M, M + QLEN, -INFINITY);

     _Float16 *   kq16_buffer          = (_Float16 *) tcm_buffer;
     _Float16 *   qv_buffer            = kq16_buffer + QLEN * DV;
